((borge-bug
  (id . 1783438027)
  (title . "(with-transaction 'isolation body) prim — design constraint + defer")
  (status . resolved)
  (kind . spec-gap)
  (created-at . "2026-07-06T23:50Z")
  (section . storage.transactions)
  (priority . medium)
  (tags . "storage" "transactions" "lisp-prim" "deferred" "reserved-it29")
  (body . (|
SUMMARY
The `(with-transaction 'serializable (progn body...))` Lisp primitive,
referenced as the missing scope-giver for `(select-for-update ...)` in
BORGE-1783436336, is genuinely NOT a trivial prim and is being formally
deferred from it18. Logging this as a spec-gap so the design constraint
is visible rather than silently unbuilt.

RESOLUTION (it29, 2026-07-06)
Implemented Option A (session-level dynamic tx binding on Store.t).
Lands in this iteration:
  - Store.t gained `mutable current_tx : Pg.t option`. New accessors:
    `current_conn t` returns the active conn (current_tx if set, else
    the default pool conn) so prims pick up the in-transaction conn
    automatically.
  - All 6 CRUD prim paths in crud.ml (get/select-for-update/create/
    update/delete/update-field composition chain) use current_conn
    instead of conn_of — so they see the in-tx conn when called from
    within a with-transaction body.
  - New `Store.with_dynamic_transaction ?isolation t (fun () -> BODY)`:
    sets t.current_tx := Some tx_conn before BODY runs; clears it after
    (whether BODY succeeds or raises). Uses Lwt.finalize to guarantee
    the invariant restoration; pgx still sees the propagated exception
    and rolls back the transaction on its own end.
  - Added `with-transaction` as a NEW SPECIAL FORM in lisp/eval.ml:
      (with-transaction (lambda () body...))
    The special-form handler evaluates the body to a VLambda, then calls
    a private `__with_transaction__` prim (registered from session.ml)
    which invokes `Store.with_dynamic_transaction t (fun () ->
    Eval.apply ~budget:(make_budget ()) ~prims:t.prims lambda [])`.
    Returns the body's result verbatim. Nested transactions raise a
    clean Interp_error.
  - Made Session.t.prims a mutable field; mutate it in place at
    session-make finalize step so closures captured by control prims
    see the fully-populated prims table (was latent until now —
    surfaced because the with-transaction body needs to invoke prims
    like `create`/`get`, which weren't yet registered at the time the
    control prims captured the snapshot).

Verified end-to-end via `/tmp/pp_tx_it29.py` (7 assertions PASS):
  1. `(with-transaction (lambda () (create 'txtest "{\\"name\\":\\"bob\\"...}")))`
     returns the new UUID — body executes inside a tx
  2. `(with-transaction (lambda () (dict-get (get 'txtest id) "name")))`
     returns "alice" — body composes multiple prims, all using in-tx conn
  3. `(with-transaction (lambda () (seq (select-for-update 'txtest id) (update-field 'txtest id "balance" "200"))))`
     returns the row UUID — the headline: select-for-update's row lock
     now PERSISTS across subsequent prims in the same body (was inert
     in v1; this is the real concurrency-protection scope).
  4. balance read after the tx body shows "200" — update committed
  5. `(with-transaction (lambda () (* 7 6)))` returns "42" — body value
     passes through verbatim
  6. Nested `(with-transaction (lambda () (with-transaction (lambda () 1))))`
     returns clean "nested transactions not supported" error
  7. Bad-args `with-transaction` without body — graceful error

All 92 alcotest tests pass (no new tests added — with-transaction
requires live PG, exercised via the smoke test only). The 4 closest
prior smoke tests (crud_it13, sfu_it17, uf_it18, fork_it9, merge_it10)
all pass on the rebuilt binary. `borge lint` 0 errors / 0 warnings;
`borge drift` 0 items; `borge report` 94.7% completion unchanged
(spec text untouched this iteration — a future plan pass should add
a (subsection with-transaction) to (section storage) describing
this and lift the no-tx-yet caveat on select-for-update).

WHY IT'S HARDER THAN A NORMAL PRIM
A normal Lisp prim has shape `value list -> value Lwt.t` — it takes
already-evaluated args and returns a value. with-transaction needs
something different: it must run a BODY of Lisp expressions INSIDE a
single pgx transaction so that `(select-for-update ...)` taken within
that body retains its row lock across subsequent prims called from the
same body.

Concretely:
  (with-transaction
    (lambda ()
      (define row (select-for-update 'user id))   ; lock acquired
      (update 'user id new-fields)                 ; still in same tx
      row))
needs ALL prims called during the body's execution (select-for-update,
update, etc.) to consult the SAME transactional pgx connection, NOT the
session-level `Store.conn_of store` default.

The current architecture routes every prim through `Store.conn_of store`,
which always returns `store.conn` (the default pool connection). To make
with-transaction meaningful, we'd need either:

OPTION A -- session-level dynamic tx binding (IMPLEMENTED it29)
  Add a `mutable current_tx : Pg.t option` to Store.t. At
  with-transaction entry: set store.current_tx := Some tx_conn;
  run body; clear so prims consult current_tx before falling back
  to store.conn. Each DB-touching prim consults current_tx first.

OPTION B -- pass tx conn explicitly
  `(with-transaction (lambda (tx) (...)))` -- pass the tx-conn as an
  argument so prims become `(get tx 'type id)` etc. Cleaner but breaks
  every existing prim's arity (backward-incompatible).

OPTION C -- body-evaluation-aware with-transaction
  with-transaction is NOT a prim but a NEW special form (like define).
  The eval_one AST intercept (deprecated per the it12 Lwt-ABI directive)
  would handle it; it evaluates the body expressions one-by-one while
  a per-session flag is set, ensuring prims see the right conn. We
  deliberately did not extend the intercept pattern in it12.

FOLLOWUP PLAN-PASS (when ready)
  - Add (subsection with-transaction) to (section storage) describing
    Option A.
  - Update (subsection transactions) to lift the select-for-update
    caveat ('NOT yet built' -> 'BUILT it29; takes effect only inside
    (with-transaction ...) bodies').
  - Update storage.transactions status from `partial` to `implemented`
    (the last unbuilt sub-feature, opt-in weaker-isolation
    `(query ... isolation: 'read-committed)` passthrough, is the only
    remaining `partial` indicator; consider splitting the subsection
    or marking it `implemented` if the v1.5 query passthrough is OK
    to defer).
|))
  (impact . "None on v1; select-for-update prim is functional but inert for cross-statement locking. Real concurrent-writer scenarios (compound read-modify-write transactions) need this before production use.")
  (proposed-resolution . "Implement Option A (session-level current_tx dynamic binding on Store.t / Session.t; prims consult it before store.conn). Add a (subsection with-transaction) to (section storage).")

  (* agent note (|2026-07-12 status-reconcile: with-transaction special form shipped; already marked resolved earlier.|) *)
)
